<!DOCTYPE html>
{{!-- Document language. Ghost has a single site locale; per-locale content is routed
     by tag and served by the locale shells (default-es.hbs, default-br.hbs), which set
     their own lang. A post in a locale collection that has no locale template renders
     with this value.
     Investigated for Phase 4a and not solvable at the layout level: a layout cannot see
     the post context (neither {{#has}} nor {{#post}} resolves), and while a
     {{#contentFor}} does reach the layout through {{{block}}}, its content is evaluated
     in the layout's context too, so a tag test there is always false. The remedy is the
     documented one: assign the locale's custom template to the post. --}}
<html lang="{{@site.locale}}" class="dark">

<head>
    {{> "head"}}
</head>

<body class="{{body_class}} bg-dark-bg text-dark-text antialiased font-sans">

    {{> "header"}}

    <main id="main-wrapper" class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-6 relative mt-4">
        {{{body}}}
    </main>
    {{> "footer"}}

    {{ghost_foot}}

    {{> "scripts"}}
</body>

</html>
